4. Apply dynamic range compression: If the audio still peaks and crackles, consider using a dynamic range compressor to control the overall level of the audio. A compressor can reduce the volume of the louder parts of the audio to prevent clipping. There are various algorithms and libraries available for dynamic range compression.

5. Experiment with different fade-in and fade-out durations: Adjusting the duration of the fade-in and fade-out periods can also affect the overall perceived loudness and the occurrence of clipping. Try shorter fade-in and fade-out durations to reduce the possibility of peaking.

